{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For I fear him.</b> A matronita asked: how could he fear Esau after the Holy One, blessed be He, had promised him? A certain Torah scholar answered with an answer from the adjacent verse, which says: ״כי במקלי עברתי את הירדן הזה״ — meaning: when the Holy One, blessed be He, promised me, I was but myself alone, and now I have become two camps. Therefore, even though I do not fear him, for the Holy One, blessed be He, promised me — nevertheless, 'I fear him, lest he come and strike me' — if [it is] upon the children, for regarding the mother and the children He did not promise me, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:24.337650524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}